Plan for the fix:
1. Add one narrow deterministic fallback rule in `legal_modal_parser.py` for U.S. Code editorial status headings (starting with patterns like `§<section> ... Repealed/Reserved/Omitted`), only when no modal cues were detected.
2. Keep it conservative by requiring U.S.C. citation context and heading-like shape checks, then emit a `frame` formula with explicit fallback metadata.
3. Add a golden parser regression test in `test_legal_modal_parser.py` for the provided sample id `us-code-18-3008-62db8e945327b1ec` and citation `18 U.S.C. 3008`, asserting that the fallback now yields a formula.
4. Run the smallest relevant test slice (`test_legal_modal_parser.py` targeted tests) and report results.
